/	PDP-8 START FOR LINC PROGRAMS

/	PDP-8 STARTUP FOR PDP-12 LINC PROGRAMS RUN FROM P?S/8 AND OS/8].

/	WRITTEN BY CHARLES LASNER P?S NY.

/	LAST EDIT:	17-AUG-2016	10:00:00	CJL

/	ASSEMBLY INSTRUCTIONS:

/	MUST BE ASSEMBLED WITH EITHER P?S/8 PAL [WITH THE '/8' COMMAND-LINE OPTION
/	SWITCH SET TO ENABLE LINC MODE ASSEMBLY] OR A FUNCTIONAL VERSION OF PAL12 FOR
/	OS/8.  NOTE: PAL12 IS A USER PROGRAM AND THERE ARE KNOWN DEFECTIVE RELEASES
/	THAT MAY BE INCAPABLE OF ASSEMBLING THIS AND OTHER RELATED LINC AND PDP-8
/	MIXED CODE PROGRAMS.  AN APPARENTLY ACCEPTABLE VERSION WAS *POSSIBLY* RELEASED
/	ON 14-AUG-1972 ACCORDING TO A SURVIVING PAPER PRINTOUT; HOWEVER, AT THE
/	PRESENT TIME, THERE ARE NO AVAILABLE MEANS TO READ THE ASSOCIATED LINCTAPE.

/	OS/8 FILE DATE CONSIDERATIONS.

/	ALL OS/8 DATES ARE SUBJECT TO THE FOLLOWING ANOMALIES.

/	1) ALL FILE DATES [IF PRESENT] CAN BE OFF BY EXACT MULTIPLES OF 8 YEARS.  A
/	   FILE APPARENTLY RELEASED ON 14-AUG-1972 COULD ACTUALLY BE FROM 14-AUG-1980,
/	   14-AUG-1988 OR 14-AUG-1996.  MANY PROGRAM FILES CREATED YEARS LATER MERELY
/	   USE FICTICIOUS DATES [SUCH AS THE OS/8 RELEASE OF THIS FILE].

/	2) MANY USERS HAVE BEEN FORCED TO ELIMINATE FILE DATES ON THEIR SYSTEMS DUE TO
/	   LACK OF DIRECTORY SLOTS, A SITUATION WHICH CAN BE SOMEWHAT ALLEVIATED BY
/	   DISABLING DATE SUPPORT.  THIS WAS OFTEN A DESPERATE DECISION MADE TO OBTAIN
/	   A SUFFICIENT QUANTITY OF FILES ON THEIR SYSTEMS; THE LOSS OF FILE DATES IS
/	   NOT A TRIVIAL MATTER.

/	3) WHEN COPYING FILES IN OS/8, IF THE TARGET DEVICE DOES NOT SUPPORT FILE
/	   DATES, OR NO CURRENT SYSTEM DATE IS SET, THE COPIED FILE WILL NOT HAVE A
/	   FILE DATE.  NOTE: THIS PROBLEM WAS PARTIALLY ALLEVIATED IN OS/278 V2 FOR
/	   DECMATES; THE DATE IS PERMANENT ONCE SET.  EVENTUALLY, THE SET DATE WILL
/	   TEND TO BECOME OUTDATED, BUT AT LEAST HAVING A SYSTEM DATE SET WILL PREVENT
/	   LOSS OF FILE DATES WHEN COPYING FILES.  ADDITIONALLY, IF OS/278 V2 IS RUN
/	   FROM MASTER MENU, THE PRESENT DATE IS PASSED TO OS/278 DIRECTLY MAKING IT
/	   FAR EASIER TO MAINTAIN A MORE ACCURATE DATE [ASSUMING THE USER SET THE
/	   PROPER DATE AND TIME WHEN THE MACHINE WAS FIRST BOOTED UP].  MASTER MENU
/	   SUPPORTS A REAL-TIME CLOCK TO ALLOW PROPER DATE INCREMENT IF THE SYSTEM
/	   RUNS INTO THE NEXT DAY.

/	4) REGARDLESS OF HOW A FILE BECAME UNDATED, IF SUBSEQUENTLY COPIED TO A SYSTEM
/	   WHERE THE DATE IS SUPPORTED [AND PRESUMABLY SET TO THE CURRENT DATE], THE
/	   CURRENT SYSTEM DATE IS APPLIED TO THE FILE; OFTEN THIS WAS TOTALLY
/	   ERRONEOUS AND MISLEADING.  NOTE: MANY PEOPLE WERE FOOLED INTO THROWING
/	   AWAY NEWER RELEASES OF PROGRAMS MERELY BECAUSE THE APPARENT DATE ON THE
/	   NEWLY RECEIVED FILE SUGGESTED IT REPLACED A FILE ALREADY PRESENT.

/	DUE TO THE ABOVE CONSIDERATIONS, ALL OS/8 DATES SHOULD BE TREATED AS
/	UNRELIABLE UNLESS THE FILE IS EXTREMELY WELL DOCUMENTED BY A RELIABLE SOURCE
/	[PREFERABLY FROM INTERNAL DOCUMENTATION WITHIN THE SOURCE CODE].
/	LINC PROGRAM STARTUP CONSIDERATIONS.

/	MANY PDP-12 PROGRAMS REQUIRING EXECUTION FROM PDP-8-BASED OPERATING SYSTEMS
/	[P?S/8 AND OS/8] ACTUALLY HAVE THEIR ROOTS IN VERSIONS WRITTEN FOR THE CLASSIC
/	LINC.  ON THAT MACHINE, PROGRAMS GENERALLY START AT EITHER 0020 OR 0400.  THE
/	OPERATING SYSTEM IS GENERALLY ABLE TO LOAD THE PROGRAMS WITH NO MEMORY
/	RESERVATIONS [OTHER THAN THE MINIMAL MEANS TO IMPLEMENT THE DESIRED STARTING
/	ADDRESS].

/	THIS IS FEASIBLE BECAUSE THESE PROGRAMS ARE ALWAYS RUN FROM LINCTAPES; DIRECT
/	HARDWARE TAPE INSTRUCTIONS ARE USED FREELY ON SUCH SYSTEMS.  AS LONG AS THE
/	PROGRAMMER CAN RESERVE THE TWO WORDS PRIOR TO EITHER STARTING ADDRESS, THE
/	OPERATING SYSTEM CAN START THE PROGRAM BY PLACING AN APPROPRIATE TWO-WORD
/	TAPE INSTRUCTION IN EITHER 0016 OR 0376 AS REQUIRED.  THESE ADDRESS VALUES ARE
/	NOT ARBITRARY.  LOCATION 0020 IS A LOGICAL STARTING POINT BECAUSE THE MEMORY
/	LOCATIONS FROM 0000-0017 HAVE SPECIAL MEANING.  IF THE PROGRAM REQUIRES
/	LOADING INTO 0016-0017, THE ALTERNATE STARTING ADDRESS OF 0400 CAN BE USED.
/	BOTH STARTING ADDRESSES ARE AVAILABLE ON THE FRONT PANEL OF ALL LINC-CLASS
/	MACHINES INCLUDING THE LINC-8 [ONLY MEANINGFUL WHEN FULL LINC SIMULATION IS IN
/	EFFECT] AND THE PDP-12.

/	ON THE CLASSIC LINC, THE PROGRAM ADDRESSES ARE ALWAYS IN THE RANGE OF
/	0000-1777 FOR THE INSTRUCTION SEGMENT [ORIGINALLY KNOWN AS THE "LOWER MEMORY
/	BANK"] AND 2000-3777 FOR THE DATA SEGMENT [ORIGINALLY KNOWN AS THE "UPPER
/	MEMORY BANK"].  THE SIGNIFICANCE OF THIS CONVENTION IS IMPORTANT: SINCE THE
/	MEMORY ASSIGNMENT IS LIMITED BY THE LINC HARDWARE, THE PROGRAM MUST START
/	WITHIN 0000-1777 BECAUSE THE DATA SEGMENT MEMORY CAN ONLY CONTAIN DATA
/	REFERENCED BY CERTAIN INSTRUCTIONS THAT SUPPORT INDIRECT ADDRESSING.

/	WITH THE RELEASE OF THE LINC-8, THE EMBEDDED PDP-8 EXTENDED MEMORY SYSTEM WAS
/	AUGMENTED TO ENHANCE MEMORY MANAGEMENT.  INSTRUCTIONS WERE ADDED CALLED "LMB"
/	[TO SET THE LOWER MEMORY BANK] AND "UMB" [TO SET THE UPPER MEMORY BANK].
/	NOTE: THESE INSTRUCTIONS ARE UNDEFINED ON THE CLASSIC LINC.  THIS ALLOWS THE
/	PROGRAMMER ADDITIONAL FLEXIBILITY IN PROGRAM LAYOUT.  A 4K LINC-8 HAS THREE
/	AVAILABLE SEGMENTS TO CHOOSE FROM.  NOTE: SEGMENT 00 IS OFF-LIMITS AS THE
/	PDP-8 CODED LINC SIMULATOR [KNOWN AS "PROGOFOP" OR PROGRAM OF OPERATION]
/	OCCUPIES MEMORY LOCATIONS 00000-01777.  ON A 4K LINC-8 THE MEMORY BANKS [LATER
/	REFERRED TO AS MEMORY SEGMENTS] COULD BE SET TO ANY VALUE FROM 01 THROUGH 03,
/	AND IF 8K IS AVAILABLE, THE ADDITIONAL VALUES 04 THROUGH 07.  NOTE: SINCE FEW
/	LINC-8 SYSTEMS WERE UPGRADED TO 8K, PREVAILING OPERATING SYSTEMS ASSUMED 4K
/	MEMORY SEGMENT ASSIGNMENT.  NOTE: ALL 8K LINC-8 SYSTEMS ARE FIELD UPGRADES.

/	MOST IMPORTANTLY, IT IS POSSIBLE TO SET THE DATA SEGMENT TO THE SAME VALUE
/	AS THE PROGRAM SEGMENT AND THEN LATER CHANGE IT TO ANY OF THE OTHER AVAILABLE
/	DATA SEGMENTS.  BY JUDICIOUS CHOICE OF INSTRUCTION SEGMENTS, IT IS POSSIBLE TO
/	WRITE PROGRAMS LARGER THAN 1K OF LINC CODE [INDEPENDENTLY OF DATA SEGMENTS].
/	RARELY DO PROGRAMS ACTUALLY REACH THESE LARGER SIZES, BUT THERE IS A FRAMEWORK
/	WITH DEFAULT STARTING CONSIDERATIONS.

/	WHILE IT IS POSSIBLE SOME EARLY "LAP" [LINC ASSEMBLY PROGRAM] OPERATING
/	SYSTEMS FOR THE LINC-8 SET DEFAULTS TO SEGMENT 01 AND 02 FOR THE INSTRUCTION
/	AND DATA SEGMENTS RESPECTIVELY, NEWER LAP SYSTEMS LOAD THE PROGRAM INTO
/	4000-5777 [SEGMENT 02], AND THE DATA INTO 6000-7777 [SEGMENT 03].
/	THIS CONVENTION IS SOMEWHAT UNFORTUNATE AS IT IS IN DIRECT CONFLICT WITH PDP-8
/	CONVENTIONS THAT RESERVE 07600-07777 FOR THE OPERATING SYSTEM.  NOTE: SOME
/	PDP-8 OPERATING SYSTEMS, SUCH AS OS/8, ALSO RESERVE 17600-17777 AND PERHAPS
/	27600-27777.  THE LAST REQUIREMENT DOES NOT APPLY AS ALL LINC-8 SYSTEMS ARE
/	LIMITED TO 4K OR 8K.  FURTHERMORE, THE MEMORY REQUIREMENTS STATED ABOVE ASSUME
/	HARDWARE MODIFICATIONS TO THE LINC-8 TO SUPPORT LINCTAPE-BASED SYSTEMS.  THERE
/	EXISTS A LINC-8 CONFIGURATION OF P?S/8 THAT RUNS ON 8K LINC-8 SYSTEMS WITHOUT
/	HARDWARE MODIFICATIONS.  NOTE: LINC-8 SYSTEMS ONLY ALLOW LINC CPU DMA
/	OPERATIONS; NO EXTERNAL DMA BUS PERIPHERALS ARE SUPPORTED.

/	THE PDP-12 DOES NOT RESTRICT THE USE OF SEGMENT 0 [00000-01777]; A TRAP
/	SIMULATOR IS ONLY USED TO SUPPORT NON-STANDARD SYSTEMS THAT SIMULATE TAPE
/	INSTRUCTIONS ON OTHER STORAGE DEVICES WHEN USING CLASSIC LINC AND LINC-8
/	OPERATING SYSTEMS.  NOTE: INCLUSION OF THE TRAP SIMULATOR DOES NOT GUARANTEE
/	ANY SPECIFIC OLDER SOFTWARE WILL FUNCTION ON A PDP-12.

/	THE PREVAILING LINC-ORIENTED SYSTEM FOR THE PDP-12 IS LAP6-DIAL OR DIAL-MS
/	[WHICH REQUIRES 8K AND OPTIONALLY SUPPORTS CERTAIN HARD DISKS].  WHILE THIS
/	OPERATING SYSTEM MAY HAVE AN INTERNAL STARTING ADDRESS IN FIELD 1 TO ACCESS
/	THE HARD DISK, THE STANDARD BOOTUP AND RESTART FOR DIAL-MS IS STILL
/	ACCOMPLISHED VIA A TWO-WORD LINCTAPE INSTRUCTION PLACED AT 04016-04017; THIS
/	MAINTAINS COMPATIBILITY WITH THE MORE WIDELY USED CONVENTION OF STARTING AT
/	04020; DIAL FORCES THE SAME LOADING CONVENTIONS PASSED DOWN FROM THE LINC-8.
/	THUS, THE DEFAULT PROGRAM SEGMENT IS 02 AND THE DEFAULT DATA SEGMENT IS 03.

/	AS LONG AS THE DESIRED PROGRAM DOES NOT CONFLICT WITH 07600-07777, IT SHOULD
/	BE POSSIBLE TO START THE LINC PROGRAM FROM THIS PROGRAM STUB [USUALLY KNOWN AS
/	"PSTART"].  PSTART IS USUALLY ASSEMBLED TO START AT 00200, THE STANDARD
/	STARTING ADDRESS FOR PDP-8 PROGRAMS.  AS LONG AS THERE IS A FREE PAGE
/	SOMEWHERE IN FIELD 0, PSTART CAN BE ASSEMBLED TO BE LOADED AND STARTED ON THE
/	AVAILABLE PAGE; HOWEVER, A GOOD WORKING KNOWLEDGE OF THE PDP-12 HARDWARE IS
/	REQUIRED TO MAKE FUNCTIONAL MODIFICATIONS TO THIS PROGRAM.

/	USAGE EXAMPLES.

/	IN THESE EXAMPLES, IT IS ASSUMED THE LINC PROGRAM IS "KALEID", THE PDP-12
/	KALEIDOSCOPE PROGRAM.

/	P?S/8 VERSION.

/	"BKALID" IS THE BINARY FILE CREATED BY ASSEMBLING THE KALEIDOSCOPE PROGRAM
/	SOURCE FILE[S].  "BPSTRT" IS THE BINARY FILE CREATED BY ASSEMBLING THIS PSTART
/	PROGRAM.

/	.GET BKALID,BPSTRT

/	.R $ [OR R %]

/	NOTE: ONCE CREATED AS DESCRIBED ABOVE, THE PROGRAM WILL CONTINUE TO FUNCTION
/	UNTIL THE "%" OR "$" FILES ON THE BOOTUP LOGICAL UNIT ARE MODIFIED.  HOWEVER,
/	A REBOOT WILL NOT IN AND OF ITSELF CHANGE ANY SYSTEM CONTENT.  AS NEEDED, THE
/	"GET" COMMAND DESCRIBED ABOVE CAN BE REPEATED TO RESTORE THE PROGRAM
/	FUNCTIONALITY.  AS SUCH, THE BINARY FILES SHOULD BE RETAINED FOR FUTURE NEEDS.
/	OS/8 VERSION.

/	DUE TO THE OS/8 DATE ANOMALIES., IT IS HIGHLY RECOMMENDED THE OS/8 DATE BE
/	SET TO THE CORRESPONDING DAY IN 1988.  THIS WILL INDICATE THE PROPER DAY OF
/	THE WEEK.  DIRECTORY LISTING FILES CAN THEN EASILY BE COSMETICALLY ALTERED BY
/	FILE EDITING TO REFLECT THE ACTUAL FILE DATES IN USE.

/	"KALEID.BN" IS THE BINARY FILE CREATED BY ASSEMBLING THE KALEIDOSCOPE PROGRAM
/	SOURCE FILE.  "PSTART.BN" IS THE BINARY FILE CREATED BY ASSEMBLING THIS
/	PROGRAM [USUALLY KNOWN AS "PSTART.PA"].

/	.R ABSLDR
/	*KALEID.BN,PSTART.BN$  [THE COMMAND LINE WAS TERMINATED WITH <ESC>.]

/	.SAVE SYS KALEID.SV;0200

/	.R KALEID

/	NOTE: IF THE OS/8 .SV FILE RESIDES ON A NON-SYSTEM DEVICE SUCH AS RKB0:, THE
/	FOLLOWING COMMAND MUST BE USED.

/	.RUN RKB0: KALEID.SV

/	NOTE: ALL DISCUSSIONS OF FILE DATES ASSUME THE DEVICE SUPPORTS ONE ADDITIONAL
/	INFORMATION WORD IN THE DIRECTORY [WHICH IS THE DEFAULT CASE].

	PMODE				/ENSURE PROPER ASSEMBLY MODE.

	IFNDEF	PROSEG	<PROSEG= 2>	/DEFAULT LINC PROGRAM SEGMENT IS 02.

	IFNDEF	DATSEG	<DATSEG= 3>	/DEFAULT LINC DATA SEGMENT IS 03.

	IFNDEF	LSTART	<LSTART= 0020>	/DEFAULT LINC STARTING ADDRESS.

	IFNDEF	PSTART	<PSTART= 0200>	/DEFAULT OVERALL STARTING ADDRESS.

	IFNDEF	REBOOT	<REBOOT= 0400>	/DEFAULT LINCTAPE RESTART ADDRESS.
/	THE PROGRAM STARTS HERE.

	FIELD	0			/THIS MUST BE TRUE.

	*PSTART				/USUALLY 00200 IF NOT MOVED.

PSTART,	NOP				/IN CASE CHAINED TO BY OS/8 OR P?S/8.
	CLA CLL				/CLEAN UP.
	IOF				/JUST IN CASE.

	ZBLOCK	3			/FOR DEBUGGING CHANGE TO THE FOLLOWING:

/	*.-3				/LOAD OVER THE ZEROED WORDS.

/	7604	/	LAS		/GET THE RIGHT SWITCHES.
/	7710	/	SPA CLA		/SKIP IF THE HIGH-ORDER BIT IS CLEAR.
/	7402	/	HLT		/ELSE HALT.

	LINC				/THE NEXT SECTION WILL BE IN LINC MODE.

	LMODE				/TELL THE ASSEMBLER ABOUT IT.

	LDF	DATSEG			/SET THE LINC USUAL DEFAULT DATA SEGMENT.
	DJR				/DON'T DESTROY LOCATION 0000 IN CASE NEEDED.
	LDA I;	20			/SET I/O PRESET BIT ONLY.
	ESF				/CLEAR THE BUS.
	LIF	PROSEG			/GOING TO THERE IN A MOMENT.
	JMP	20			/THE USUAL LINC STARTING ADDRESS.  CHANGE THIS
					/AS NECESSARY.

	PMODE				/BACK TO GOODY MODE.
	PAGE				/GET TO NEXT PAGE.

/	THE FOLLOWING CODE IS PROVIDED IN CASE THE RUNNING LINC MODE PROGRAM MANAGES
/	TO SCREW UP THE BOOTSTRAP.  IT ONLY WORKS ON PDP-12 LINCTAPE VERSIONS OF BOTH
/	P?S/8 AND OS/8.

REBOOT,	CLA CLL				/CLEAN UP
	IOF				/MAKE SURE NO INTERRUPT PROBLEMS.
	CDF	00			/ENSURE FIELD 0.
	TAD	TAPE1			/GET "RDC" INSTRUCTION.
	DCA I	L4016/(4016)		/STORE WHERE IT IS NEEDED.
/	TAD	 TAPE2			/GET TAPE BLOCK WORD [USUALLY 0000].
	DCA I	L4017/(4017)		/STORE JUST BEFORE 0020 IN THAT SEGMENT.
	LINC				/THE NEXT SECTION WILL BE IN LINC MODE.

	LMODE				/TELL THE ASSEMBLER ABOUT IT.

	LDF	03			/DEFINITE LINC STARTING CONDITIONS FOR REBOOT.
	LIF	02			/LIKEWISE FOR PROGRAM SEGMENT.
	JMP	16			/WHERE THE BOOT CODE IS.

/	LINC MODE INSTRUCTION CONSTANTS.

TAPE1,	RDC				/READ AND CHECK TAPE BLOCK INSTRUCTION.
TAPE2,	0				/THIS SHOULDN'T BE NEEDED.

	PMODE				/BACK TO GOODY MODE.

/	THE FOLLOWING DEFINITIONS ARE DONE THIS WAY FOR THE BENEFIT OF FEEBLE
/	ASSEMBLERS SUCH AS THE LAP6-DIAL OR DIAL-MS ASSEMBLERS THAT DO NOT SUPPORT
/	PDP-8 LITERALS.

L4016,	4016				/ADDRESS CONSTANT 4016.
L4017,	4017				/ADDRESS CONSTANT 4017.

	$				/THAT'S ALL FOLK!
